WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:04.565
Jupiter is the fifth planet from the Sun, and the largest in the Solar System.

00:05.019 --> 00:15.654
It is a gas giant with a mass nearly 2.5 times that of all the other planets in the Solar System combined and slightly less than one-thousandth the mass of the Sun.

00:16.140 --> 00:21.116
The diameter of Jupiter is 11 times that of Earth and a tenth that of the Sun.

00:21.577 --> 00:32.077
It orbits the Sun at a distance of 5.20 AU (778.5 Gm), with an orbital period of 11.86 years.

00:32.677 --> 00:41.584
Jupiter is the third-brightest natural object in the Earth's night sky, after the Moon and Venus, and has been observed since prehistoric times.
